UID:20270624-RentGuidelinesBoardfinalvote@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270624
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Rent Guidelines Board final vote
DESCRIPTION:The rent adjustment for roughly a million rent-stabilized apa
 rtments\, for leases beginning October 2027. Date estimated from recent 
 practice (June 17\, 2024\; June 30\, 2025\; June 25\, 2026).\n\nhttps://
 rentguidelinesboard.cityofnewyork.us/
URL:https://rentguidelinesboard.cityofnewyork.us/
CATEGORIES:housing
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270630-Fiscal2028budgetadoption@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Fiscal 2028 budget adoption
DESCRIPTION:The Charter's trigger date is June 5 (section 254)\, but in p
 ractice adoption lands at the end of June: the fiscal 2027 deal was stru
 ck and voted on June 30\, 2026\, hours before the deadline. Date estimat
 ed from that practice.\n\nhttps://council.nyc.gov/budget/
URL:https://council.nyc.gov/budget/
CATEGORIES:budget
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270704-SlaveryendsinNewYorkState200thanniversar@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270704
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270705
SUMMARY:Slavery ends in New York State — 200th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:An 1817 law took full effect on July 4\, 1827\, ending legal 
 slavery in New York and freeing thousands of remaining enslaved people.\
 n\nhttps://history.nycourts.gov/when-did-slavery-end-in-new-york/
URL:https://history.nycourts.gov/when-did-slavery-end-in-new-york/
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270713-Theblackoutthatbrokethecitysspirit50than@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270714
SUMMARY:The blackout that broke the city's spirit — 50th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:Lightning strikes knocked out power for some 25 hours\, unlea
 shing widespread looting and arson across the crime-plagued\, cash-strap
 ped city.\n\nhttps://www.britannica.com/event/New-York-City-blackout-of-
 1977
URL:https://www.britannica.com/event/New-York-City-blackout-of-1977
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270728-SilentParademarchesdownFifthAvenue110tha@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270728
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270729
SUMMARY:Silent Parade marches down Fifth Avenue — 110th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:Thousands of Black New Yorkers marched in silence down Fifth 
 Avenue to protest lynchings and the East St. Louis massacre.\n\nhttps://
 guides.loc.gov/chronicling-america-silent-protest-parade
URL:https://guides.loc.gov/chronicling-america-silent-protest-parade
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270810-TheSonofSamiscaptured50thanniversary@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270811
SUMMARY:The Son of Sam is captured — 50th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:Police arrested David Berkowitz\, ending a serial-killing spr
 ee that terrorized the city for more than a year.\n\nhttps://www.britann
 ica.com/biography/David-Berkowitz
URL:https://www.britannica.com/biography/David-Berkowitz
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20271012-CiticorpCenteropensthenissecretlyreinfor@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271013
SUMMARY:Citicorp Center opens\, then is secretly reinforced — 50th annive
 rsary
DESCRIPTION:Hugh Stubbins and engineer William LeMessurier completed Citi
 corp Center\, a 59-story tower on stilts with a distinctive sloped top. 
 A year later a hidden structural flaw prompted a secret emergency repair
 .\n\nhttps://www.enr.com/articles/60648-author-details-citicorp-tower-de
 sign-error-and-the-race-to-fix-it
URL:https://www.enr.com/articles/60648-author-details-citicorp-tower-desi
 gn-error-and-the-race-to-fix-it
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20271017-JosephPappsPublicTheateropenswithHair60t@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271018
SUMMARY:Joseph Papp's Public Theater opens with "Hair" — 60th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:Joseph Papp opened his year-round Public Theater in the forme
 r Astor Library on Lafayette Street\, launching it with the rock musical
  "Hair\," the first production in its new home.\n\nhttps://www.villagepr
 eservation.org/2016/10/17/ground-breaking-musical-hair-premiers-at-the-p
 ublic-theater-october-17-1967/
URL:https://www.villagepreservation.org/2016/10/17/ground-breaking-musica
 l-hair-premiers-at-the-public-theater-october-17-1967/
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20271031-TruckattackonHudsonRiverbikepath10thanni@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271101
SUMMARY:Truck attack on Hudson River bike path — 10th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:A man drove a rented truck down a Lower Manhattan bike path\,
  killing eight people and injuring many others. It was the city's deadli
 est terrorist attack since 9/11.\n\nhttps://www.justice.gov/archives/opa
 /pr/sayfullo-saipov-charged-terrorism-and-murder-aid-racketeering-connec
 tion-lower-manhattan
URL:https://www.justice.gov/archives/opa/pr/sayfullo-saipov-charged-terro
 rism-and-murder-aid-racketeering-connection-lower-manhattan
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20271102-TheAfricanFreeSchoolopens240thanniversar@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271103
SUMMARY:The African Free School opens — 240th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:The Manumission Society opened the African Free School\, the 
 first school in New York for the children of enslaved and free Black fam
 ilies.\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Free_School
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Free_School
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20271108-EdKochiselectedmayor50thanniversary@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Ed Koch is elected mayor — 50th anniversary
DESCRIPTION:The brash congressman won the mayoralty\, beginning three ter
 ms that spanned the city's recovery from fiscal collapse.\n\nhttps://www
 .britannica.com/biography/Ed-Koch
URL:https://www.britannica.com/biography/Ed-Koch
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
